# tiberius: the strata engine's local patch, against upstream ffa80d73 (v0.2.10, engine 0.1.56).
# REBASED 2026-11-03 onto ffa80d73.  Two hunk conflicts in generate.cpp, both resolved by keeping both
# sides: upstream's new `keep_sync()` at the request-ending pin release (it waits on the idle drafter's
# queued upkeep, so the pins are released after it), and the `use_mtp` -> `draft_on` rename in the
# `drafted` guard, where our refill-timing join is kept around upstream's variable.  Everything else
# applied cleanly.  0.2.10's expert_source changes (the ArenaExpertSource #4846 RAM fallback and the
# Windows standby-list release) sit outside this patch's FileExpertSource region, and the ggml pin is
# unchanged (third_party/ggml/VERSION.txt), so nothing under third_party/ggml moved.
#
# ADDED 2026-11-04: change 3 (the transactional park) was written on top of that rebase; park_source()
# and conversation_cache.hpp are outside every region changes 1-2 touch (the cache header was not in
# this patch before it), so it needs no merge.  The whole patch was regenerated against ffa80d73 and
# re-applied in order onto a pristine tree (byte-identical result; transcript in
# /tmp/strata-tune/park-patch.md).  Built on tiberius
# (/nix/store/3qla1qfa09rsf6rqmcnnndk04hrqvb0y-strata-engine-0.1.56) and probed against the deployed
# pre-fix binary: the pre-fix arm evicted two parked conversations and the next request re-read the
# prompt their copy held; the patched arm skipped with "nothing evicted, 2 still parked" and restored
# it (normal parks unchanged, all six answer shas identical).  Deployed as generation 101 on 2026-11-04
# (system 07pr3sndmbszvsyq8jayd334ak0nwf59).
#
# ADDED 2026-11-04 (second addition): STRATA_DAX_TIMING, log-only per-rotation timing of the DAX window:
# one line per rotation with the stream-drain wait and the unregister/register driver times (off by
# default; the copy and the window are the same either way).  It exists because the DAX rotation is the
# prompt path's remaining fixed cost: 9 windows per 46.84 GiB pack pass, each a drain plus an
# unregister/register of ~5.5 GiB.  Measured with it on the patched build (single-window path): wait
# 108-198 ms + unregister 65-87 ms + register 125-342 ms, i.e. 310-630 ms per rotation.
# The two-window pipelined rotation the timing was built to judge (a run of ~2-3 layers per registration,
# two windows resident, the next run registered while the current one still streams) was measured in the
# task-8 A/B and REJECTED: on the 4,260/8,276-token reads it was +1.66%/+4.13% slower (the run cap
# doubles the rotation count from 9 to 19 per pass; the fence wait is 0 ms, but an unregister that lands
# while the copy engine is active costs 60-260 ms, not the 21.5 ms it costs after a drain), while the
# 26,134-token read gained 5.43% (its
# rotations hide under the compute-bound timeline) but its answer sha changed with the arm (the frozen
# window's size moves the decode's PCIe grouping).  Only the log-only timing is kept.
#
#
# ADDED 2026-11-04 (third addition, round 5): the streamed session RESTORE and the DFlash2 invalidate-after-restore.
#   * `session_file_restore_streamed` (conversation_file.{hpp,cpp}): pass 1 validates the file (header, identity,
#     bounds, whole payload hash) and parses only its metadata; pass 2 re-reads the same fd and streams every K/V
#     part straight into its pool through a SessionKvSink, materialising only the two running-state copies.  The
#     restore's host peak at 250k tokens drops from 3,727 MiB (the whole image) to ~270-276 MiB (session_stream_peak_bytes:
#     two state copies + two 16 MiB read blocks + ~2 MiB of transient metadata), so the 250k
#     conversation can be restored on this 8 GB box at all (the RAM preflight refused it before).  Format v1 is
#     untouched - additive API only: old files parse identically, old engines read files this engine writes.
#     A refusal in pass 1 (or from the caller's prepare step) leaves the device untouched; a failure after the
#     first sink write reports SessionStatus::touched and the caller exits the engine (never decode a partial state).
#   * the DFlash2 drafter is invalidated after a successful RESTORE, before live_ok = true: the file's K/V is not
#     the drafter's lineage log and a restore can rewind a conversation it has seen, so its position/tags are
#     stale (answers stay verified either way; without it acceptance collapses after a rewind).
#   Unit tests (conversation_file_test: streamed image == session_file_read, corrupt/truncated refused in pass 1
#   before any sink, injected sink failure -> touched, the exact peak formula, a layers-only draft-optional file) pass;
#   design and validation matrix: /tmp/strata-tune/stream-restore-design.md.
#   * SAVE and RESTORE are draft-optional (found in the first validation window): the deployed lane runs DFlash2 with
#   NO --mtp, so SAVE's unconditional mtp.kv_state() was an empty state and every SAVE was refused with
#   "conversation snapshot: invalid K/V extent" - disk sessions had never worked on this lane (the empty sessions
#   directory was the symptom).  SAVE now records the QSA layers only when no MTP draft layer is loaded (nullable
#   draft through conversation_snapshot_sources), and RESTORE reads layers-only files through nullable draft in
#   conversation_session_read_limits/validate_meta/stream_sinks/stream_finish.  A lane with the MTP layer keeps the
#   layers+1 format byte-identical; a file with the other layer count is refused (config identity already separates
#   the lanes).  Format v1 untouched.
#
# REGENERATED 2026-11-05 (round 6, HYGIENE ONLY): the four "payload ends early" over-read guards that the 1128b6c9
# build carried in conversation_file.cpp (In::raw, In::skip, and both spans of stream_impl's K/V stream_part) were
# accidentally dropped by a debug-instrumentation strip while fixing the streamed restore before 829b20ec; they are
# restored here verbatim (a span that exceeds the remaining payload bytes is refused at once instead of relying only
# on the final left!=0 / IO check), and conversation_file.cpp's final newline is restored.  Nothing else changes: the
# streamed RESTORE, the draft-optional SAVE/RESTORE and the df2.reset() after a restore are byte-identical to
# 829b20ec (verified against the deployed tree: only that file's guard lines differ).
#
# ROUND 7 (pmem park spill, tiberius local change): the conversation cache keeps the RAM park path byte-identical; a
# park the transactional pre-check (or the parked-cache budget) refuses is written as a v1 session file on /optane by
# the existing SAVE writer (K/V streamed from the pools, live + deepest checkpoint) and inserted into a separate,
# metadata-only file tier (ids/images/used, no state, no K/V).  The next turn restores such a park with the round-5
# streamed RESTORE, then invalidates the DFlash2 drafter like a disk restore.  The file tier has its own --conversation-
# park-dir/-mib/-slots/-min-free-mib settings and its own LRU (only file entries are evicted; RAM parks are never
# evicted for a file; the park donor is handed back before the file write).  No cudaHostRegister: park files travel
# through the writer's 16 MiB block.  Zero format change (v1), zero answer change; a refused/failed park or a restore
# refused in pass 1 stays non-destructive (transactional contract), a fatal after the first K/V sink write keeps the
# existing ERR+exit path.  Boot re-admission of existing park files is NOT in this cut (in-run tier only).
#
# ROUND 8b (CUDA stop bound + per-window telemetry counters, tiberius local change): (a) upstream #4677's stop bound
# (a verify window that would commit past an EOS inside it commits to the stop token) is ported from HIP to CUDA by
# removing the STRATA_USE_HIP guards on serve_stop_bound's include, its one definition and both call sites; the HIP
# path is the same code, and STRATA_SERVE_STOP_BOUND=0 still disables it.  (b) every finished request prints one
# `WSTAT` line (counters only, no answer change) with its DAX rotations (counted where the rotation happens, whatever
# source object performs it), the prompt path's borrowed device bytes, verify windows/rows/accepted rows, windows by
# size, the stop-bound clips, the prompt read seconds and, when STRATA_PREFILL_TIMING=1, the prefill phase timeline;
# serve/server.py parses it in every request reader (the solo GEN loop, the batch/admission _control loop,
# _drain_control), stashes it across the DONE parse that replaces a request's figures (attached by _parse_done, reset
# at every request start so nothing is inherited), and exposes it on /metrics/prometheus (the llama.cpp-named endpoint,
# additive strata:* counters plus the verify-window histogram and prefill phase families) and on
# /metrics?format=prometheus / the JSON totals via serve/prometheus.py; serve/test_wstat.py pins the parse -> DONE ->
# totals/renderer chain on the host.  Purely additive to /metrics; answer bytes, tokens and stop behaviour on the
# normal cells are unchanged.
#
# Four changes, in one patch because the first two interleave in the same regions of
# expert_source.{hpp,cpp}, prefill.{hpp,cpp} and generate.cpp; changes 3-4 are independent (the park fix:
# one function in generate.cpp + two methods in conversation_cache.hpp; the streamed restore:
# conversation_file.{hpp,cpp}, conversation_snapshot.{hpp,cpp}, conversation_state.cpp, the restore block in
# generate.cpp, and conversation_file_test.cpp).  Changes 1-2 are local and opt-in through their own env var -
# nothing they add runs unless the module sets it.  Change 3 is always on and only changes what a REFUSED park
# does: an admitted park behaves exactly as before.  Change 4 is always on and only changes the RESTORE path
# (plus the drafter invalidation after it): SAVE, served requests and an admitted park are the old code.
#
# 1. STRATA_REGISTER_DAX, the sliding DAX window.  cudaHostRegister cannot pin
#    the 46.84 GiB pack (the driver caps a process's total registered host memory
#    at ~7 GiB, measured), so the engine registers a 6 GiB window of whole
#    page-aligned layers over the mmap'd pack and slides it as the prefill walk
#    advances; every layer the window holds is DMA-able straight out of DAX, which
#    removes the CPU staging path.  Measured 2026-10-02 on the real corpus:
#    prefill 12,325 -> 9,527 ms (-22.7%) for a 4292-token prompt.
#    STRATA_REGISTER_DAX_MIB is the window budget (6144 is the measured ceiling:
#    6912 registers and 7168 is refused, so the 8 rotations per prompt are
#    irreducible).
# 2. STRATA_REFILL_PIN_SRC, the decode-time VRAM refill read from registered
#    sources: the adaptive tier's 2 MiB copies were 98% pageable at ~0.87 ms each
#    and sat on the decode loop's critical path.  The patch resolves a batch's
#    sources first, merges their page-rounded spans, registers them (ReadOnly |
#    Portable) and releases them once the batch's event has landed.  Measured
#    2026-10-02, counterbalanced, 8 runs/arm: decode +12.2% / +7.1% / +5.9% on
#    three cells, refill join 18.04 -> 1.46 ms per window.
# 3. The transactional park (park_source, generate.cpp).  The physical-RAM admission gate used to run
#    `while (!admit() && ... evict_oldest())` BEFORE it knew whether the park could be admitted, so a
#    REFUSED park had already evicted up to slots() parked conversations (production: "need 994 MiB plus
#    384 MiB floor, 1102 MiB available; evicted 2, 0 still parked" - two good conversations destroyed by
#    a park that never happened; 126 refusals in one 8 h run, 893 in the log), and the retained-K/V donor
#    (take_reuse_for) was consumed by the same refusal.  Now the gate is checked ONCE before make_room()
#    and before any eviction, against available + the bytes every evictable parked conversation would
#    return (ConversationCache::evictable_bytes); a park that could not fit even with the cache emptied
#    is skipped with "nothing evicted, N still parked" and the donor is handed back
#    (ConversationCache::give_reuse).  A park that CAN fit takes the old eviction loop unchanged; its
#    refusal is now reachable only when RAM changed between the pre-check and the loop.  No upstream
#    counterpart: #4677 fixes a different, HIP-only stop-bound park bug (see default.nix).
#
# Two hardening pieces ride with the pin, both needed by this box:
#   * the straddle guard: a span that PARTLY overlaps an existing registration is
#     dropped, not registered (the driver refuses a copy whose source begins inside
#     one registration and ends outside it), and a refused exchange staging drops
#     that swap instead of failing the request (upstream aborts).
#   * the register/unregister bookkeeping is per request, so no pin outlives it.
#
# REBASED 2026-10-27 onto 5e8a4cca (v0.2.7).  Upstream rewrote the adaptive refill
# between 0.2.4.2 and 0.2.7 (the "resolve every swap first" plans pass, the
# nib::guard_raw instrumentation, the batch H2D path), so the two largest hunks
# were re-merged by hand: the plans pass now carries our pin classification
# (BlobClass) and the batch registration, and upstream's nib guard is kept inside
# our loop.  The serve path and the generate path each carry a copy, as before.

